== benchmark 1-71
     1	# Recorded results and benchmark evidence
     2	
     3	Status: **no qualified native MPC-versus-baseline performance result**.
     4	Historical serving measurements, CPU tests and current component diagnostics
     5	are intentionally separate. No new experiment was run to write this document.
     6	
     7	## E1: historical native serving measurements, not MPC
     8	
     9	Hardware/configuration as recorded by the runner: RTX 4090, reported 24,564 MiB,
    10	driver 595.91.07; configured model Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507; runner environment
    11	vLLM 0.30.0, Torch 2.13.0+cu130, Python 3.12.3. The manifests explicitly say
    12	these package records are not proof of the remote backend version and do not
    13	observe backend launch provenance; the historical report states the same core
    14	runtime versions.
    15	Both captures replay the same Azure-derived arrivals/input lengths with
    16	synthetic prompts, output cap 128, context 8192 and 300-second arrival windows.
    17	Source output lengths are not replayed. TTFT SLO is 0.5 seconds.
    18	
    19	| Capture | Offered | Completed success | Rejected | Failed | SLO-good completions | SLO goodput (req/s) | Client TTFT p99 (s) |
    20	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
    21	| Shared A | 7,643 | 1,976 | 5,667 | 0 | 572 | 1.906667 | 2.412583 |
    22	| Shared B | 7,643 | 2,059 | 5,584 | 0 | 736 | 2.453333 | 2.202635 |
    23	
    24	TTFT p99 is conditional on successful requests; rejection is shown alongside
    25	it. SLO goodput counts eventual successful completions whose first content
    26	meets the scheduled-arrival TTFT deadline, divided by offered duration.
    27	The arrival window is not total wall time including startup/drain.
    28	
    29	These are **scheduled identification captures on different hosts**, with
    30	different protocol declarations, budget-schedule orders, replay-plan hashes
    31	and gateway virtual-environment paths. They are not MPC, Fixed/OneMove
    32	comparisons, causal schedule effects or proof of an optimal cap.
    33	Historical integrity/load/control qualification does not mean every request
    34	met its SLO. Recorded `git_dirty=true` is retained; source hashes, not a claim
    35	of a pristine checkout, support the archived runtime identity.
    36	
    37	### E1 evidence chain and reconstruction limits
    38	
    39	| Item | Exact evidence |
    40	|---|---|
    41	| Reports | [A report](../results/shared-client-20261018/captures/shared-client-a-r1/report.json), [B report](../results/shared-client-20261018/captures/shared-client-b-r1/report.json) |
    42	| Configuration and trace identity | [A manifest](../results/shared-client-20261018/captures/shared-client-a-r1/manifest.json), [B manifest](../results/shared-client-20261018/captures/shared-client-b-r1/manifest.json) |
    43	| Complete raw archives and file hashes | [Raw-bundle index](../results/shared-client-20261018/raw-bundle/index.json); browsing subsets are not complete raw captures |
    44	| Trace SHA256 | `62f3f182bcb889c846b5a46a05a53766ef20c5f79008e9050a4fe33707bc4e2e` |
    45	| Archived independent audits | [verification.json](../results/shared-client-20261018/verification.json) |
    46	| Exact collection declarations and commands | [Historical report](../results/shared-client-20261018/report.md), [A runbook](../experiments/shared-client-qualification-v1.md), [B runbook](../experiments/shared-client-b-v1.md) |
    47	| Recorded runtime commit | `d0ccb2c0d3711e1b2a69bb4ec248c61961ce3586` |
    48	| Evidence publication commit | `aea7694a0af2d1dadc883b4b9e33d1a9bdb61098` |
    49	
    50	Historical offline feature/forecast reconstruction command, after using the
    51	report's extraction helper and recorded analysis environment:
    52	
    53	```bash
    54	python results/shared-client-20261018/reproduce.py \
    55	  --raw-root /tmp/shared-client-captures \
    56	  --output-dir /tmp/shared-client-analysis --extended \
    57	  --code-root /path/to/recorded-runtime-source
    58	```
    59	
    60	This command does not regenerate the E1 outcome table. `reproduce.py` checks
    61	the 15 manifest-recorded runtime files, then runs `identification_features.py`
    62	and `forecast_baselines.py` from `--code-root` without checking their hashes.
    63	It is not a fully source-pinned reproduction path. E1 table reconstruction
    64	evidence is the archived raw-to-report comparison in `verification.json`,
    65	not a fresh replay performed for these documents.
    66	
    67	The runtime commit was not resolvable in the current local object database
    68	during this documentation audit. A source tree matching the archived hashes is
    69	required; the example path is a required input, not a working shipped checkout.
    70	This is a P0 portability gap. No dependencies were installed and no captures
    71	were re-extracted/replayed for this documentation change.
